# Schema naming: single source of truth

**DONE.** Closed before these files carried a status word. The `.done`
suffix is the record; this line is that same answer in the second place
the check reads, and no new judgement.

Review finding 7. _resp() exists in three copies (grpc_schema.py,
server.py, remote.py); a rename breaks dispatch only at first RPC.
StrMsg/Int64Msg/BoolMsg are declared but never referenced; server
decode's scalar branch applies message-shaped conversion to plain
scalars (works by coincidence).

Fix: grpc_schema owns all naming and the type->message map; server and
client import it; delete unused messages.

## Done 2026-08-25

Closed alongside the wire-codec unification, which needed the same
thing.

grpc_schema now holds one function per naming rule (service_name,
req_name, resp_name, method_path, value_msg_name), and annotate()
stamps the results INTO the manifest before it is written. server and
remote read `m["rpc"]["path"|"req"|"resp"]`; neither rebuilds a name.
A rename now reaches both sides at build time.

StrMsg/BoolMsg/Int64Msg are gone. The scalar branch is gone with them:
WireCodec classifies by manifest policy rather than by message shape.
